<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madinat ash-Sha'b</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Al Ittihad, Al-Ittihad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madinat ash-Sha'b is a town on the western side of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, built from 1959 as Al Ittihad, the purpose-built capital of the British-sponsored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federation-of-arab-emirates-of-the-south">Federation of Arab Emirates of the South</a> and its successor, the Federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a>. It housed the federal council and ministries. After the British withdrawal and the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> in 1967 it was renamed Madinat ash-Sha'b, the People's City.</p></div>
